{
  "version": "0.7.2-beta.3",
  "notes": "## Changes since `v0.7.2-beta.2`\n\n### Features\n\n- send COLORTERM=truecolor to SSH servers: remote TUIs saw only TERM=xterm-256color and quantized to 256 colors; the env request goes with the PTY and a server whose AcceptEnv does not list it just ignores it ([1747808f](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/1747808fd7826e29a24edee4312220f1c6a5f846))\n\n### Fixes\n\n- let xterm.js answer OSC 10/11 color queries over SSH: the backend replied with a fixed light gray and dark gray, so programs like Codex blended their panels from colors unrelated to the tab's theme; xterm.js answers with the tab's own theme, as it already does for local sessions ([332a9e18](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/332a9e1843be6ad2f3feb7a3d4d0a54b986a2ee5))\n- stop the WebGL renderer painting opaque boxes behind dim text under window blur: xterm's addon-webgl draws a background rectangle for any cell whose bg word is non-zero, and dim, italic and link flags live in that word, so dim text on the default background got the theme color painted opaque over the transparent terminal; a Vite transform rewrites that check to ignore default-colored backgrounds and fails the build if an upgraded addon no longer has the code ([2ff396d8](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/2ff396d8821c07dcdcb408a5d25d4b968035f1e9))\n- Fix Windows terminal theme queries with bundled ConPTY ([f7ad3e41](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/f7ad3e41f80e23170fcc9be94504b7f95bc0ddcc))\n\n### Other changes\n\n- list the bundled ConPTY under Open Source Licenses: the Windows build ships Microsoft's MIT-licensed ConPTY, so the About dialog shows its notice, with the version read from prepare-conpty.ps1 so the two stay in step ([5b4a4660](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/5b4a4660a214ff42e4b26f4bde7d816bf6da44cb))\n- log which ConPTY local terminals use on Windows: portable-pty falls back to the system ConPTY without a word when the bundled conpty.dll is missing, and the older system ones drop the color queries TUIs send at startup, so the first local terminal says which one it got ([d809fd86](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/d809fd86dd2934169491fe32b95e32254d2a305c))\n\n**Full comparison:** [v0.7.2-beta.2...v0.7.2-beta.3](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/compare/v0.7.2-beta.2...v0.7.2-beta.3)",
